{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:bcfc9712f256269e","name":"A519 Invader Close Support Starfighter","source":{"id":"source:reference-bcfc9712f256269e","title":"A519 Invader Close Support Starfighter","revision":15599,"timestamp":"2024-08-18T00:52:51Z","sha256":"3f9c5bf2dd31029436b5cee97ac9dc0bd75d80a12aba1bc97a919cf3ac38a700","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=15599","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=A519%20Invader%20Close%20Support%20Starfighter&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-bcfc9712f256269e","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Legacy Era Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Legacy_Era_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Affiliations: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Black Sun"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Black_Sun","referenceId":"reference:5c22b34bff28e06d"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The A519 Invader from Kuat Drive Yards is designed for planetary, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Space Station"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Space_Station"},", and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Capital Ship"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Capital_Ship"}," invasion scenarios requiring close support for ground troops, zero-g boarding parties, and dropship and assault shuttle escort. Mercenary and heavily armed law enforcement units are the ship's initial customers, but it isn't long before the A519 starts turning up in pirate fleets and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Black Sun"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Black_Sun","referenceId":"reference:5c22b34bff28e06d"}," intimidation forces.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The Invader packs a punch with its two Twin ",{"tag":"a","children":["Laser Cannons"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Laser_Cannons"},", especially when configured to fire in a focused area. The system allows any ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle Pilot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle_Pilot","referenceId":"reference:4aff6d0e54fff36e"}," to use the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Burst Fire"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Burst_Fire","referenceId":"reference:ff3da4756d0ccd5c"}," feat when firing at a target at Short or Point-Blank ",{"tag":"a","children":["Range"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Range"},". In addition, the attack penalty is reduced from -5 to -2 for pilots who already have the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Burst Fire"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Burst_Fire","referenceId":"reference:ff3da4756d0ccd5c"}," feat. Pilots with ",{"tag":"a","children":["Burst Fire"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Burst_Fire","referenceId":"reference:ff3da4756d0ccd5c"}," can also use it for attacks at greater ",{"tag":"a","children":["Ranges"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Ranges"},", but do not benefit from the additional damage indicated below.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The Invader is equipped with heavy-duty shielding and hardened alloy armor plating to improve its durability. For such a small fighter, these upgrades cost the ship maneuverability, and the Invader is at a distinct disadvantage with dogfighting with top-of-the-line ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starfighters"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starfighters","referenceId":"reference:e127af2636e147fc"},".\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Default (Skilled)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["A519 Invader Close Support Starfighter Statistics (CL 8)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Huge ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starfighter"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starfighter"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +8; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"referenc